From 65d2eeea8315942fcc324b4f3dd4dd98c1a072ad Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: forge-shepherd <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Sat, 11 Jul 2026 13:06:36 +0530
Subject: [PATCH] feat(kernel): populate stage_runs so workflow phase is real
 (f61601ab)
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

The kernel_stage_runs table existed in schema.js but nothing wrote to it,
so the dashboard/`show` guessed workflow phase from status+claim — a
claimed-open issue with a merged PR still showed "dev". This wires the
table with a direct-registry capability (mirroring the worktree registry).

Kernel (lib/kernel/sqlite-driver.js):
- recordStageRun({issue_id, stage, action:start|complete, substage?, now?}):
  idempotent per (issue_id, stage). start opens an active row; complete
  stamps completed_at + status=done on the same row (creating it if the
  stage was never explicitly started).
- listStageRuns({issue_id}) ordered by started_at.
- getCurrentStage({issue_id}): latest ACTIVE run, else latest COMPLETED,
  else null.
- `show` now returns current_stage + current_stage_status from stage_runs
  so consumers read the real phase instead of guessing.

CLI (lib/commands/stage.js): `forge stage <id> <stage> --start|--complete`,
plus `--current` / `--list` reads and `--json`. Resolves issue-id prefixes.
Stage vocabulary validated against lib/workflow/stages.js (STAGE_IDS).

Deferred to follow-up 5a5ba3a6: auto-wiring each stage command
(/plan /dev /validate /ship /review /verify) to call this, and the
dashboard consuming current_stage. Supersedes the a2279f65 "missing field"
framing — the table already existed, it was just unpopulated.

Tests: test/kernel/stage-runs.test.js (record start/complete, idempotency,
active>completed resolution, show integration) + test/commands/stage.test.js
(verb start/complete/current/list, validation, json, prefix resolution).

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.8 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>
